    "user_request_original": "Design a defect-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate. Stack topology: air incident medium, then 8 repeated pairs of MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) and al2o3 (MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) first from air side), followed by a single MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) defect cavity layer, then 8 repeated pairs of al2o3 and MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) (al2o2 first), terminating on SiO2 (Gao) substrate. Total film layers: 17. All 17 layer thicknesses are optimizable design variables. Wavelength bands: maximize transmittance in 255-280 nm, minimize transmittance in 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm. No metal layers. Normal incidence, unpolarized light. Total layers must not exceed 30.",
